@@ -156,12 +159,18 @@ Not present: any module other than `identity`, `appService`, `incidents`, `alert
 31. **Delayed jobs have no outbox row, so no dead-letter row.** On exhaustion (`JOBS_EXECUTION_ATTEMPTS`, same backoff) the failure state is an `error` log `delayed_job_failed`. At-least-once is guaranteed by the scanner, not the job: the DB record decides, a milestone stays a scan candidate until its `Notification` key exists, and the loop retries a failing pass without a limit (tested: all attempts fail, the next scan records the milestone). A deterministic failure (for example a `NotificationContractError`) is therefore retried and logged on every scan. Changes outside the slice's own location (minimum contracts): `src/infra/jobs` (delayed scheduling, registry, wrapper, runtime routing), `appService/index.ts` exports `policyUserViolations`, `notifications/index.ts` exports `deriveIdempotencyKey`. Test changes to existing suites: none.
